<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">15 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 15 February, from 706 to 1965.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-ii" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/justinian-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">706 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,320 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Justinian II has his predecessors executed in the Hippodrome</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-ii">Justinian II</a>, restored to the throne in 705 with the help of a Bulgarian army, had his predecessors Leontius and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiberius">Tiberius</a> III publicly executed in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hippodrome-of-constantinople">Hippodrome of Constantinople</a>. Both had reigned after his deposition in 695.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/justinian-ii">Justinian II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hippodrome-of-constantinople">Hippodrome of Constantinople</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1002">1002 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,024 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Arduin of Ivrea is crowned king of Italy at Pavia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At an assembly of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> nobles at Pavia, Arduin, margrave of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivrea">Ivrea</a>, was crowned King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> after the death of Emperor Otto III. Opposed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> and by the German king Henry II, he held out until 1014.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arduin-of-ivrea">Arduin of Ivrea</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1113 CE <span class="tih-ago">913 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope Paschal II recognises the Knights Hospitaller</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The bull Pie postulatio voluntatis placed the hospital of St John in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> under papal protection. The order later took on a military role and survives today as the Sovereign Military Order of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malta">Malta</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1493">1493 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">533 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Christopher Columbus writes his letter on the first voyage</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Aboard the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caravel">caravel</a> Niña on the return leg, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a> wrote the first known document announcing the completion of his first voyage across the Atlantic. A postscript was added on his arrival in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a> on 4 March.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1564">1564 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">462 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Galileo Galilei is born in Pisa</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galileo-galilei">Galileo</a>'s telescopic discoveries, including Jupiter's moons, and his studies of motion made him a founder of modern physics. His defence of Copernicus brought his trial by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-inquisition">Inquisition</a> in 1633.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1898">1898 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">128 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">USS Maine explodes in Havana harbour</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An explosion sank the American battleship, killing some 260 men. The cause is still debated, but US newspapers blamed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, and the cry 'Remember the Maine' helped bring war in April.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1942">1942 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">84 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Singapore surrenders to Japan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">General Arthur Percival surrendered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a>, and some 80,000 British, Indian and Australian troops became prisoners. Churchill called it the worst disaster and largest capitulation in British history.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1961">1961 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">65 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US figure skating team killed in the Sabena air crash</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Sabena Flight 548 crashed on approach to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brussels">Brussels</a>, killing all 72 aboard and a man on the ground. Among the dead was the entire US figure skating team, en route to the world championships in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1965">1965 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">61 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Canada raises its Maple Leaf flag</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The red and white Maple Leaf flag was raised on Parliament Hill in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottawa">Ottawa</a>, replacing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canadian-red-ensign">Canadian Red Ensign</a>. 15 February is now marked as National Flag of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a> Day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 15 February <span class="n">11</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ladislaus-of-naples"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ladislaus-of-naples.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Ladislaus of Naples</span><span class="tp">1377–1414</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/piero-di-lorenzo-de-medici"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/piero-di-lorenzo-de-medici.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Piero di Lorenzo de' Medici</span><span class="tp">1472–1503</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/juliana-of-stolberg"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/juliana-of-stolberg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Juliana of Stolberg</span><span class="tp">1506–1580</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pedro-menendez-de-aviles"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pedro-menendez-de-aviles.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pedro Menéndez de Avilés</span><span class="tp">1519–1574</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/galileo-galilei"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/galileo-galilei.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Galileo Galilei</span><span class="tp">1564–1642</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/paul-de-chomedey-de-maisonneuve"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/paul-de-chomedey-de-maisonneuve.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Paul de Chomedey de Maisonneuve</span><span class="tp">1612–1676</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/louis-xv"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/louis-xv.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Louis XV</span><span class="tp">1710–1774</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/domingo-faustino-sarmiento"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/domingo-faustino-sarmiento.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Domingo Faustino Sarmiento</span><span class="tp">1811–1888</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/susan-b-anthony"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/susan-b-anthony.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Susan B. Anthony</span><span class="tp">1820–1906</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/robert-ley"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/robert-ley.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Robert Ley</span><span class="tp">1890–1945</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/milo-dukanovic"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Milo Đukanović</span><span class="tp">b. 1962</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
